// =============================================================================
// _tod_elite_hp.gsc — over-head HEALTH BARS ON EVERY ELITE (2026-09-25, docs/174)
//
// User: "the elites on this map will have a health bar above them so players
// know how much health they have left ... this applies to only elites ... do
// something similar to how we did on Hellbound ... I would prefer if the
// health bars were white." And, same session: "the bar does need some kind of
// nice animation ... when it gets hit, it should tick and then go down ... a
// small little pulse, nothing crazy ... it shouldn't be tiny."
//
// THIS IS HELLBOUND'S `_tod_zombie_hp.gsc` (its docs/49, route A), NARROWED TO
// ELITES AND RE-THEMED. It REVERSES this map's 2026-08-19 "They wont have
// healthbars or anything" rule (the notes in _tod_bosses / _tod_boss_fx are
// updated in the same change so nobody "fixes" the bars back out).
//
// ROUTE A — server-only waypoint hudelems, ZERO clientfield bits:
//   NewClientHudElem( player ) + SetShader( mat, w, h ) + SetWaypoint( true )
//   + SetTargetEnt( elite )
// = the stock entity-head-icon recipe (entityheadicons_shared.gsc:159-185),
// live-proven on zombie actors by map 0 and played four times on Hellbound.
// The bar is ONE elem per elite per player whose FILL is an image swap through
// pre-baked materials (tod_hpbar_e_NN for elites, tod_hpbar_b_NN for the
// Dealer (the boss bar), tod_hpbar_s_NN for the Necromancer's helpers,
// NN = tenths, plus _h1/_h2 edge-pulse frames), generated by
// tools/gen_hpbar_art.js into source_data/tod_hud_bars.gdt: e/b RED, s WHITE.
//
// THREE MAP-0 TRAPS THIS CODE IS SHAPED AROUND (all live-verified 2026-06-13):
//   1. SetShader RESETS the waypoint anchor — apply() re-issues SetWaypoint +
//      SetTargetEnt in the same frame after every SetShader, no wait between.
//   2. Two waypoint elems at one anchor draw as ONE — so frame, track and fill
//      are baked into a single image; health is the image swap.
//   3. hud::create* factories parent to the screen layer and silently ignore
//      SetTargetEnt — this file never touches hud_util_shared.
//
// WHAT "ELITE" MEANS HERE (is_elite): anything that carries the map's boss
// triad or a kind tag — the Doppelghast, the Mangler and the Dealer today (the
// Panzer, Rogue Protector, Apothicon Fury, hellhound, armored sprinter and the
// Keeper retired whole 2026-10-05, with their rows). Ordinary zombies NEVER get a
// bar: no scan ever deals one to an actor without those marks, and the damage
// callback returns before creating anything for them. Every elite family in
// this map sets its marks ON THE SPAWN FRAME (each spawner's own TRAP 3 note),
// so the discovery scan cannot see an elite as a zombie first.
//
// PERSISTENT, WITH A SPAWN-IN GRACE: an elite's bar lives from spawn-in to
// death (no hit-linger — the user wants to "know how much health they have
// left", not only while shooting). It is NOT dealt until the actor is
// actually in: the Doppelghast and Mangler are Ghost()ed for a 1.2 s tell, the
// Dealer arrives through his portal. Per-kind grace in grace_ms(); a real hit
// ends the grace early (if you can hit it, you may see it).
//
// RED FOR ENEMIES, WHITE FOR THE NECROMANCER'S HELPERS (user 2026-10-01: "the
// elites on this map have a white bar above them that needs to be changed to red.
// And then the necromancers summoners need to have the white bar. So you can tell
// the difference and you can see how much health they have left"). Every elite
// and boss wears a RED bar (sets e / b); every helper a Necromancer summons — a
// thrall, a soul hound, the Mangler (tod_necro_helper, _tod_necro_summon) —
// wears a smaller WHITE bar (set s), seen by every player, so a black helper
// Mangler can never be mistaken for the enemy one. Nothing on the horde's side
// hurts a helper, so its bar is what is LEFT of it: the helper publishes
// tod_hpbar_frac (its life clock, and a thrall's kills — whichever runs out
// first) and the bar draws the smaller of that and real health. A helper's bar
// steps down in tenths and its edge pulses on every step, so the last seconds
// are visible. Helpers have their OWN bar budget (TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_BUDGET): a
// screen full of helpers can never take a bar from an elite.
//
// HIT ANIMATION: ONLY THE LEADING EDGE of the remaining health pulses — a
// white-hot notch that swells past the frame and settles, like a hit marker.
// Baked into two hit frames per fill step; the element is never resized.
// Details at the TOD_HPBAR_HIT_* block. (The first build, 2026-09-25 20:59,
// punched the WHOLE bar; the user asked for the edge only.)
//
// BUDGET. The server hudelem pool is shared, fixed-size and unmeasured. Worst
// case here is one elem per elite per client; the map's elite roof is small
// (TOD_ELITE_ROOF_ALL + the hunters' cap), so the budget below is
// generous, but it is still a HARD ceiling: a bar past it is simply not dealt
// until one ends (dev log DENY). level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi is the number to
// read at 4 players.
//
// OWNERSHIP. Each bar is run by a LEVEL thread (never a thread ON the actor)
// holding a player-keyed elem array, so it survives the actor being Delete()d
// (the Fall's seal reclaim, relocate_entrance, corpse cleanup) and still
// destroys every elem — the "breaks when teleported" failure the All-around
// Enhancement mod admits to.
//
// KNOWN LIMITS (Hellbound docs/49 §3): draws through walls, shows the engine's
// off-screen edge arrow, constant on-screen size (SetWaypoint(true); false =
// sized in 3D — one flag to A/B).
//
// DEV LOGS: [TOD_HPBAR] INIT / DEAL / DENY / BAR / END / POOL_FULL / SUMMARY
// (30 s) in console_mp.log when level.tod_dev is armed. Every DEAL / BAR / END
// carries set=e|b|s (s = a WHITE helper bar); BAR on a helper also carries
// owner= and the published frac=.
// =============================================================================

#using scripts\shared\flag_shared;
#using scripts\zm\_zm_spawner;

#insert scripts\shared\shared.gsh;

// These 93 materials ship in source_data/tod_hud_bars.gdt + 186 zone lines
// (tools/gen_hpbar_art.js writes both and docs/174_elite_hpbar_art/
// precache_lines.txt, which is this block; tools/test_elite_hp.js proves the
// lists agree). Per set: 11 rest frames (_00.._10) + 20 hit frames (_NN_h1/_h2).
// Sets: e = elite (RED), b = boss (RED), s = the Necromancer's helpers (WHITE).
// A precache for a material not in the fastfile is a load error — pull all
// three together or none.
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_00" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_01" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_01_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_01_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_02" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_02_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_02_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_03" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_03_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_03_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_04" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_04_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_04_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_05" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_05_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_05_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_06" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_06_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_06_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_07" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_07_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_07_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_08" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_08_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_08_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_09" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_09_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_09_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_10" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_10_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_e_10_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_00" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_01" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_01_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_01_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_02" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_02_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_02_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_03" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_03_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_03_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_04" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_04_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_04_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_05" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_05_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_05_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_06" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_06_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_06_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_07" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_07_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_07_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_08" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_08_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_08_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_09" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_09_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_09_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_10" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_10_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_b_10_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_00" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_01" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_01_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_01_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_02" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_02_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_02_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_03" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_03_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_03_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_04" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_04_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_04_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_05" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_05_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_05_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_06" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_06_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_06_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_07" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_07_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_07_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_08" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_08_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_08_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_09" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_09_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_09_h2" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_10" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_10_h1" );
#precache( "material", "tod_hpbar_s_10_h2" );

#namespace tod_elite_hp;

#define TOD_HPBAR_ENABLED     1      // 0 = the module inits and does nothing (the A/B)

// Draw sizes, in hudelem units (x3 = px at 1080p). BIGGER since the first play
// (user 2026-09-25: "It's too small ... both height and width"): the bar body
// went 48x6 -> 76x10 units. These are the CANVAS sizes, which include the
// transparent margin the hit pulse swells into — they MUST equal the source
// PNG size / 4 (tools/gen_hpbar_art.js prints them; tools/test_elite_hp.js
// checks them), or the art is stretched. Resize in the generator, not here.
#define TOD_HPBAR_W           84     // elite canvas 336x72 px source (bar body 76x10 units = 228x30 px @1080p)
#define TOD_HPBAR_H           18
#define TOD_HPBAR_BOSS_W      136    // the boss (Dealer) canvas 544x80 (bar body 128x12 units = 384x36 px)
#define TOD_HPBAR_BOSS_H      20
#define TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_W    72     // the Necromancer's helpers (WHITE) canvas 288x64 (bar body 64x8 units = 192x24 px)
#define TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_H    16

// Budget (hudelems across ALL clients) and the per-bar cap derived from it:
// solo 96, 2p 48, 3p 32, 4p 24 concurrent bars. Elites never come close.
#define TOD_HPBAR_ELEM_BUDGET 96
#define TOD_HPBAR_CAP_MIN     8
// The Necromancer's helpers have their OWN budget, so helpers never take a bar
// from an elite: up to 6 helpers per Necromancer (3 + 2 SUMMONING POWER slots,
// or the Mangler + hounds) -> solo 6 bars, 4 Necromancers at 4p = 24 helpers
// against a cap of 16 (the rest are dealt as others end; dev log DENY).
// Module total: 96 + 64 = 160 elems.
#define TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_BUDGET 64
#define TOD_HPBAR_SCAN        0.15   // discovery scan period (s)
#define TOD_HPBAR_TICK        0.1    // per-bar update period (s)
#define TOD_HPBAR_STEPS       10     // eleven images = tenths

// SPAWN-IN GRACE per kind (ms from first sighting; a hit ends it early).
#define TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_MS         1500   // the fallback
#define TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_TELL_MS    1700   // Doppelghast + Mangler: TOD_*_TELL_SECS 1.2 s ghosted + 0.5 s
#define TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_SUMMON_MS  600    // a helper: the soul burst it rises from (hound_think's soul body lands at 0.3 s)

// ===========================================================================
// BAR HEIGHT IS PER KIND (Hellbound's 2026-09-17 lesson: "they all have
// different heights"). Units above the actor origin. Grounding: the zombie,
// Mangler and Doppelghast all ask for setPhysParams( 15, 0, 72 ), so the
// Mangler/Doppelghast bars sit a hair over a zombie's head. (The Panzer, Rogue
// Protector, Fury, hellhound, armored sprinter and Keeper rows retired whole
// with them, 2026-10-05.)
// FIRST PASS — each is one #define and a -GscOnly build; the dev log prints
// `kind=` and `zoff=` on every bar so a report names the exact line.
// ===========================================================================
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_DOPPEL    74     // black robot Doppelghast
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_MANGLER   76     // 72 box + helmet
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_BOSS      90     // an elite with no row of its own
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_DEALER    110    // THE DEALER (docs/199): the Keeper's skeleton, levitating 14 in in state one
// THE NECROMANCER'S HELPERS (WHITE bars) — a thrall wears the charcoal body (the
// retired armored sprinter's played 66), the soul hound is the stock dog (the
// retired hellhound's played 30), the helper Mangler is the Mangler.
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_THRALL    66
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_SOULHOUND 30
#define TOD_HPBAR_Z_HELPER_MANGLER 76

// HIT ANIMATION — ONLY THE EDGE PULSES (user 2026-09-25, after the first play:
// "when I hit the enemy, the whole bar pulses. I just want the right side of the
// remaining health to pulse ... like a little hit marker ... just that little
// edge"). The first build scaled the WHOLE element on a hit; a waypoint hudelem
// can only be scaled whole, so the edge pulse is BAKED into the art instead:
// every fill step has two hit frames (tod_hpbar_<e|b>_NN_h1 small, _h2 peak)
// where only the fill's leading edge swells past the frame and glows — frame,
// track and the rest of the fill are pixel-identical to the rest frame. On a
// health drop the bar shows the NEW fill level at _h2 for TOD_HPBAR_HIT_PEAK
// frames, then _h1, then rest. The element's size never changes.
#define TOD_HPBAR_HIT_FRAMES     6      // frames the pulse lasts (x HIT_TICK = 0.3 s)
#define TOD_HPBAR_HIT_PEAK       3      // of those, how many show the peak (_h2); the rest show _h1
#define TOD_HPBAR_HIT_TICK       0.05   // per-bar tick while a pulse is running (one server frame)

#define TOD_HPBAR_SUMMARY_SCANS  200    // dev SUMMARY every N scans (200 x 0.15 s = 30 s)

function init()
{
	level.tod_hpbar_live     = 0;   // ELITE bars currently managed (RED, sets e / b)
	level.tod_hpbar_summon_live = 0;   // HELPER bars currently managed (WHITE, set s)
	level.tod_hpbar_elems    = 0;   // live hudelems this module owns, all clients
	level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi = 0;   // high-water mark — the pool question

	dev_log( "INIT enabled=" + TOD_HPBAR_ENABLED + " budget=" + TOD_HPBAR_ELEM_BUDGET + " summon_budget=" + TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_BUDGET + " cap_min=" + TOD_HPBAR_CAP_MIN
		+ " hit_frames=" + TOD_HPBAR_HIT_FRAMES + " hit_peak=" + TOD_HPBAR_HIT_PEAK + " w=" + TOD_HPBAR_W + " h=" + TOD_HPBAR_H
		+ " summon_w=" + TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_W + " summon_h=" + TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_H + " colours=elite_red,helper_white" );

	if ( !TOD_HPBAR_ENABLED )
		return;

	// A hit ends the spawn-in grace and stamps the drop frame. Stock
	// zombie_damage() runs every registered callback on every hit
	// (_zm_spawner.gsc:2095-2121); returning false leaves the damage path
	// untouched. Elites whose damage bypasses zombie_damage() are covered by the
	// health poll in manage() — the edge pulse keys on the health DROP, not on this.
	zm_spawner::register_zombie_damage_callback( &on_zombie_damage );

	level thread scan_loop();
}

// Concurrent bar ceiling for the current player count (see the BUDGET note).
// summon = the helpers' own budget.
function cap( summon )
{
	n = GetPlayers().size;
	if ( n < 1 )
		n = 1;
	budget = TOD_HPBAR_ELEM_BUDGET;
	if ( IS_TRUE( summon ) )
		budget = TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_BUDGET;
	c = int( budget / n );
	if ( c < TOD_HPBAR_CAP_MIN )
		c = TOD_HPBAR_CAP_MIN;
	return c;
}

// PUBLIC — the one definition of "elite" this module uses. Every elite family
// in this map stamps at least one of these on its spawn frame. A Necromancer's
// helper is NEVER an elite here, whatever it carries (it wears the WHITE bar).
function is_elite( z )
{
	if ( is_summon( z ) )
		return false;
	if ( isdefined( z.tod_boss_kind ) )
		return true;
	return IS_TRUE( z.is_boss );
}

// PUBLIC — a Necromancer's helper (thrall / soul hound / Mangler), stamped by
// _tod_necro_summon::helper_register on the frame it becomes one. WHITE bar.
function is_summon( z )
{
	return IS_TRUE( z.tod_necro_helper );
}

// PUBLIC — which height / grace row this actor uses. Most specific first.
function bar_kind( z )
{
	if ( is_summon( z ) )
	{
		if ( isdefined( z.tod_necro_kind ) )
			return "summon_" + z.tod_necro_kind;   // summon_thrall / summon_hound / summon_mangler
		return "summon_thrall";
	}
	if ( isdefined( z.tod_boss_kind ) )
		return z.tod_boss_kind;              // doppelghast / mangler / dealer
	return "boss";
}

// The wide bar is for the boss: the Dealer, the final boss (docs/199). (The
// Panzer and the Keeper wore it too until they retired whole, 2026-10-05.)
function is_wide( kind )
{
	return ( kind == "dealer" );
}

function bar_zoff( kind )
{
	switch ( kind )
	{
		case "doppelghast": return TOD_HPBAR_Z_DOPPEL;
		case "mangler":     return TOD_HPBAR_Z_MANGLER;
		case "dealer":      return TOD_HPBAR_Z_DEALER;
		case "summon_thrall":  return TOD_HPBAR_Z_THRALL;
		case "summon_hound":   return TOD_HPBAR_Z_SOULHOUND;
		case "summon_mangler": return TOD_HPBAR_Z_HELPER_MANGLER;
	}
	return TOD_HPBAR_Z_BOSS;
}

function grace_ms( kind )
{
	switch ( kind )
	{
		case "doppelghast":
		case "mangler":
		case "dealer":      return TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_TELL_MS;   // the Dealer arrives through the Keeper's 1.3 s portal
		case "summon_thrall":
		case "summon_hound":
		case "summon_mangler": return TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_SUMMON_MS;
	}
	return TOD_HPBAR_GRACE_MS;
}

// self = the damaged actor. MUST return false: true would claim the damage and
// stop stock's own handling (_zm_spawner.gsc:1926/2055). Non-elites return
// before anything is created.
function on_zombie_damage( mod, hit_location, hit_origin, player, amount, weapon, direction_vec, tagName, modelName, partName, dFlags, inflictor, chargeLevel )
{
	if ( isdefined( self ) && IsAlive( self ) && isdefined( self.health ) && ( is_elite( self ) || is_summon( self ) ) )
	{
		self.tod_hpbar_hit_ms = GetTime();
		try_deal( self, true );
	}
	return false;
}

// The single dealer. from_hit = the hit itself is the evidence (grace waived).
function try_deal( z, from_hit )
{
	if ( IS_TRUE( z.tod_hpbar_managed ) )
		return;
	if ( !isdefined( z.tod_hpbar_first_ms ) )
		z.tod_hpbar_first_ms = GetTime();   // first sighting (within one scan of spawn)
	kind = bar_kind( z );
	summon = is_summon( z );
	if ( !from_hit && ( GetTime() - z.tod_hpbar_first_ms ) < grace_ms( kind ) )
		return;                             // still spawning in
	live = level.tod_hpbar_live;
	if ( summon )
		live = level.tod_hpbar_summon_live;
	if ( live >= cap( summon ) )
	{
		if ( !IS_TRUE( z.tod_hpbar_denied ) )
		{
			z.tod_hpbar_denied = true;      // log once per actor, retry every scan
			dev_log( "DENY ent=" + z GetEntityNumber() + " kind=" + kind + " summon=" + summon + " why=cap live=" + live + " cap=" + cap( summon ) );
		}
		return;
	}
	if ( summon )
		level.tod_hpbar_summon_live++;
	else
		level.tod_hpbar_live++;
	dev_log( "DEAL ent=" + z GetEntityNumber() + " kind=" + kind + " set=" + set_tag( kind, summon ) + " from_hit=" + from_hit + " hp=" + z.health
		+ " live=" + level.tod_hpbar_live + " summon_live=" + level.tod_hpbar_summon_live + " elems=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems );
	z.tod_hpbar_managed = true;
	level thread manage( z, kind, summon );
}

// Discovery: every live axis actor that is an elite, and every live allied
// actor that is a Necromancer's helper, is handed to try_deal, which applies
// the grace. Ordinary zombies are skipped by is_elite; partners and every
// other ally by is_summon.
function scan_loop()
{
	level endon( "end_game" );
	level flag::wait_till( "initial_blackscreen_passed" );

	scans = 0;
	for ( ;; )
	{
		team = "axis";
		if ( isdefined( level.zombie_team ) )
			team = level.zombie_team;

		ai = GetAITeamArray( team );
		for ( i = 0; i < ai.size; i++ )
		{
			z = ai[ i ];
			if ( !isdefined( z ) || !IsAlive( z ) || !isdefined( z.health ) )
				continue;
			if ( IS_TRUE( z.tod_hpbar_managed ) )
				continue;
			if ( !is_elite( z ) )
				continue;
			try_deal( z, false );
		}

		// THE NECROMANCER'S HELPERS are on "allies" (thrall_make / spawn_hound /
		// spawn_mangler set it on the spawn frame), so the axis array never sees them.
		helpers = GetAITeamArray( "allies" );
		for ( i = 0; i < helpers.size; i++ )
		{
			h = helpers[ i ];
			if ( !isdefined( h ) || !IsAlive( h ) || !isdefined( h.health ) )
				continue;
			if ( IS_TRUE( h.tod_hpbar_managed ) )
				continue;
			if ( !is_summon( h ) )
				continue;
			try_deal( h, false );
		}

		scans++;
		if ( scans >= TOD_HPBAR_SUMMARY_SCANS )
		{
			scans = 0;
			dev_log( "SUMMARY ai=" + ai.size + " live=" + level.tod_hpbar_live + " summon_live=" + level.tod_hpbar_summon_live
				+ " elems=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems + " hi=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi + " cap=" + cap( false ) + " summon_cap=" + cap( true )
				+ " players=" + GetPlayers().size );
		}
		wait TOD_HPBAR_SCAN;
	}
}

// One bar (one elem per connected player) for one elite or helper, until it
// dies or is removed. summon = a Necromancer's helper (WHITE set s).
function manage( z, kind, summon )
{
	level endon( "end_game" );

	elems  = [];   // player entnum -> hudelem
	owners = [];   // player entnum -> player entity (reads undefined once they leave)

	wide   = ( !summon && is_wide( kind ) );
	art_set = set_tag( kind, summon );
	zoff   = bar_zoff( kind );
	w = TOD_HPBAR_W;
	h = TOD_HPBAR_H;
	if ( wide )
	{
		w = TOD_HPBAR_BOSS_W;
		h = TOD_HPBAR_BOSS_H;
	}
	if ( summon )
	{
		w = TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_W;
		h = TOD_HPBAR_SUMMON_H;
	}
	entnum = z GetEntityNumber();
	if ( summon )
		dev_log( "BAR ent=" + entnum + " kind=" + kind + " set=" + art_set + " zoff=" + zoff + " hp=" + z.health
			+ " owner=" + ( isdefined( z.tod_necro_owner ) ? z.tod_necro_owner GetEntityNumber() : -1 )
			+ " frac=" + ( isdefined( z.tod_hpbar_frac ) ? z.tod_hpbar_frac : -1 ) );
	else
		dev_log( "BAR ent=" + entnum + " kind=" + kind + " set=" + art_set + " zoff=" + zoff + " wide=" + wide + " hp=" + z.health );

	// Denominator: maxhealth when the family set one (they all do, on the spawn
	// frame), else the highest health seen. Re-read every tick — the sprinter's
	// promotion rescales both fields under a running bar.
	maxhp = z.health;
	if ( isdefined( z.maxhealth ) && z.maxhealth > maxhp )
		maxhp = z.maxhealth;
	if ( maxhp < 1 )
		maxhp = 1;

	hit      = 0;       // pulse frames left to draw
	was_anim = false;   // last frame was a pulse frame (the settle frame must redraw)
	why      = "gone";
	last_hp  = z.health;
	last_q   = -1;      // the last drawn tenth (a helper's edge pulses on every step down)
	last_mat = "";

	while ( isdefined( z ) && IsAlive( z ) && isdefined( z.health ) )
	{
		hp = z.health;
		if ( isdefined( z.maxhealth ) && z.maxhealth > 0 )
			maxhp = z.maxhealth;
		if ( hp > maxhp )
			maxhp = hp;

		frac = hp / maxhp;
		// A HELPER'S bar is what is LEFT of it: _tod_necro_summon publishes its life
		// clock (and a thrall's kills) as tod_hpbar_frac; the smaller of that and
		// real health is drawn.
		if ( summon && isdefined( z.tod_hpbar_frac ) && z.tod_hpbar_frac < frac )
			frac = z.tod_hpbar_frac;
		if ( frac < 0 )
			frac = 0;
		if ( frac > 1 )
			frac = 1;
		q = int( frac * TOD_HPBAR_STEPS + 0.5 );
		if ( q < 1 && hp > 0 )
			q = 1;                            // alive = never an empty bar (and always an edge to pulse)

		if ( hp < last_hp )
			hit = TOD_HPBAR_HIT_FRAMES;       // every drop re-pulses the edge (the user's "tick")
		if ( summon && last_q >= 0 && q < last_q )
			hit = TOD_HPBAR_HIT_FRAMES;       // a helper ticks down a step: the same edge pulse
		last_hp = hp;
		last_q  = q;

		// The pulse: peak frames first, then the small frame, then rest. Only the
		// IMAGE changes; the element's size never does (the edge swell is baked).
		stage = 0;
		pulsing = ( hit > 0 );
		if ( pulsing )
		{
			stage = 1;
			if ( hit > ( TOD_HPBAR_HIT_FRAMES - TOD_HPBAR_HIT_PEAK ) )
				stage = 2;
			hit--;
		}
		mat = art_material( art_set, q, stage );
		col = ( 1, 1, 1 );                    // never tint the art
		changed  = ( mat != last_mat ) || was_anim;
		was_anim = pulsing;
		last_mat = mat;

		// Drop entries whose owner left — the engine freed their elems.
		keys = GetArrayKeys( elems );
		for ( i = 0; i < keys.size; i++ )
		{
			k = keys[ i ];
			if ( !isdefined( owners[ k ] ) && isdefined( elems[ k ] ) )
			{
				elems[ k ] = undefined;
				level.tod_hpbar_elems--;
			}
		}

		// One elem per connected player; late joiners get theirs on the next tick.
		players = GetPlayers();
		for ( i = 0; i < players.size; i++ )
		{
			p = players[ i ];
			if ( !isdefined( p ) || !IsPlayer( p ) )
				continue;
			key = p GetEntityNumber();
			fresh = false;
			if ( !isdefined( owners[ key ] ) || !isdefined( elems[ key ] ) )
			{
				e = make_elem( p, zoff );
				if ( !isdefined( e ) )
				{
					if ( !IS_TRUE( level.tod_hpbar_pool_logged ) )
					{
						level.tod_hpbar_pool_logged = true;
						dev_log( "POOL_FULL ent=" + entnum + " elems=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems + " hi=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi + " live=" + level.tod_hpbar_live );
					}
					continue;   // retried next tick, never throws
				}
				elems[ key ]  = e;
				owners[ key ] = p;
				fresh = true;
			}
			if ( changed || fresh )
				apply( elems[ key ], z, zoff, mat, w, h, col );
			// THE HUD VEIL, server half (docs/187 cards, docs/188 the Item Shop
			// spin): while a full-screen moment owns THIS player's screen their
			// copy of every bar hides. Alpha only - SetShader is what resets the
			// waypoint anchor (trap 1), so this never touches the anchor.
			want_a = 0.92;
			if ( IS_TRUE( p.tod_menu_frozen ) || IS_TRUE( p.tod_solo_upg_active ) )
				want_a = 0;
			if ( elems[ key ].alpha != want_a )
				elems[ key ].alpha = want_a;
		}

		if ( pulsing )
			wait TOD_HPBAR_HIT_TICK;     // one server frame per pulse step
		else
			wait TOD_HPBAR_TICK;
	}

	// Teardown — runs whether the actor died or was Delete()d (z undefined).
	if ( why == "gone" && isdefined( z ) )
		why = "dead";
	keys = GetArrayKeys( elems );
	for ( i = 0; i < keys.size; i++ )
	{
		k = keys[ i ];
		if ( isdefined( owners[ k ] ) && isdefined( elems[ k ] ) )
		{
			elems[ k ] Destroy();
			level.tod_hpbar_elems--;
		}
	}
	if ( summon )
		level.tod_hpbar_summon_live--;
	else
		level.tod_hpbar_live--;
	dev_log( "END ent=" + entnum + " kind=" + kind + " set=" + art_set + " why=" + why + " live=" + level.tod_hpbar_live
		+ " summon_live=" + level.tod_hpbar_summon_live + " elems=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems + " hi=" + level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi );
	if ( isdefined( z ) )
		z.tod_hpbar_managed = undefined;
}

// Raw NewClientHudElem — never a hud::create* factory (trap 3 in the header).
// Returns undefined when the server hudelem pool is full; callers must guard.
function make_elem( player, zoff )
{
	e = NewClientHudElem( player );
	if ( !isdefined( e ) )
		return undefined;
	e.archived       = false;
	e.hidewheninmenu = true;
	e.x = 0;
	e.y = 0;
	e.z = zoff;
	e.alpha = 0.92;
	e.sort  = 1;
	level.tod_hpbar_elems++;
	if ( level.tod_hpbar_elems > level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi )
		level.tod_hpbar_elems_hi = level.tod_hpbar_elems;
	return e;
}

// Which art set a bar draws: s = a Necromancer's helper (WHITE), b = the wide
// boss bar (RED), e = every other elite (RED).
function set_tag( kind, summon )
{
	if ( IS_TRUE( summon ) )
		return "s";
	if ( is_wide( kind ) )
		return "b";
	return "e";
}

// tod_hpbar_<e|b|s>_<NN>[_h1|_h2] — the generated art's material names. stage 0 =
// rest, 1 = small pulse, 2 = peak pulse. An empty bar (00) has no hit frames.
function art_material( art_set, tenths, stage )
{
	prefix = "tod_hpbar_" + art_set + "_";
	if ( tenths < 0 )
		tenths = 0;
	if ( tenths > 10 )
		tenths = 10;
	name = prefix + tenths;
	if ( tenths < 10 )
		name = prefix + "0" + tenths;
	if ( stage > 0 && tenths > 0 )
		name = name + "_h" + stage;
	return name;
}

// Size + tint + RE-ANCHOR, all in one frame (trap 1 in the header).
function apply( e, z, zoff, mat, w, h, col )
{
	if ( !isdefined( e ) || !isdefined( z ) )
		return;
	e.color = col;
	e SetShader( mat, w, h );
	e.x = 0;
	e.y = 0;
	e.z = zoff;
	e SetWaypoint( true );      // true = constant on-screen size; false = sized in 3D
	e SetTargetEnt( z );
}

// Dev-mode diagnostics (CLAUDE.md pattern): gated on the compile-time tod_dev
// flag, string assembled OUTSIDE the developer block, PrintLn INSIDE it.
function dev_log( msg )
{
	if ( !( IS_TRUE( level.tod_dev ) || IS_TRUE( level.tod_diag ) ) )
		return;
	line = "[TOD_HPBAR] ms=" + GetTime() + " " + msg;
	/#
	PrintLn( line );
	#/
}
